{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"agent_message","text":"The direct kernel’s best large tile is now within ~17% of rocBLAS, but direct tiling cannot efficiently cover the shortest rows. I’m adding a split-K path for those cases: several programs compute disjoint FP32 K-ranges into a temporary buffer, followed by one reduction. This trades a small write/reduction for enough parallel work to use the whole GPU."}}
