{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"agent_message","text":"Split-K reaches parity only for the very shortest cases; once M grows past roughly 256, rocBLAS’s projection kernel wins despite the copy. I’m now testing wider 16-wave direct tiles, which should reduce per-thread accumulator pressure and let the fused path keep more matrix instructions in flight on CDNA4. If they do not clear rocBLAS, I’ll retain the reference-style path for the affected shapes rather than ship a slower custom kernel."}}
