{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"agent_message","text":"`torch.compile` is numerically exact and improves eager latency by about 4–5% (0.088 vs 0.092 ms small, 0.952 vs 0.995 ms large). The remaining avoidable cost is the generic transpose copy. I’m replacing only that copy with a layout-aware Triton kernel and leaving the projection to rocBLAS, which is already the fastest GEMM implementation here."}}
