{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_54","type":"agent_message","text":"A useful hardware asymmetry showed up: rocBLAS is ~3% faster for large M when the left operand is column-major (0.864 vs 0.894 ms at M=4096). I’m testing a tiled transpose-copy that emits that layout directly. It only needs to keep its extra transpose cost below ~30 μs to improve the verified large cases."}}
