{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_61","type":"agent_message","text":"The column-major path pays off cleanly for the aligned large workloads: about 0.461 ms vs 0.474 ms at M=2048 and 0.919 ms vs 0.95–0.96 ms at M=4096, with exact outputs across every batch/sequence factorization. I’m enabling it only for aligned power-of-two M; ragged and smaller shapes keep the faster row-major path."}}
